Platform: the raptorlake-nvidia host (i9-13900T, UHD 770 0xa780 on i915, two
NVIDIA RTX Ada GPUs, kernel 6.6) with a stale GuC: the distro's linux-firmware
predates i915/tgl_guc_70.bin, so i915 fell back to i915/tgl_guc_70.1.1.bin and
runs GuC 70.1.1 where the driver wants 70.5.1. The firmware gatekeeper must
refuse every GPU engine on the iGPU with a one-line fix, and plan() must fall
back to a green cell on a usable target (the P-cores, or the NVIDIA GPUs).

Derived from tests/fixtures/raptorlake-nvidia (copied unedited) with two changes:
- usr/lib/firmware/i915/tgl_guc_70.bin.xz removed (the older linux-firmware).
- sys/kernel/debug/dri/0/gt0/uc/guc_info and huc_info added, in the form
  tests/fixtures/capture.sh writes (the driver's header, not the register dump).

Where the debugfs records come from:
- Format: intel_uc_fw_dump() in drivers/gpu/drm/i915/gt/uc/intel_uc_fw.c (Linux
  v6.6 and v7.3-rc7): "GuC firmware: <selected>", "GuC firmware wanted: <path>"
  when the selected file is not the wanted one, "status:", then "version: wanted
  W, found X" when X is older than W.
- Why the fallback: v6.6's INTEL_GUC_FIRMWARE_DEFS lists ALDERLAKE_S (Raptor
  Lake-S is its subplatform) as guc_maj(tgl, 70, 5, 1), then guc_mmp(tgl, 70, 1,
  1), then guc_mmp(tgl, 69, 0, 3). intel_uc_fw_fetch() walks down that list on
  -ENOENT and keeps the ideal file and version as "wanted"; an older minor still
  loads and runs ("is recommended, but only ... was found").
- Sizes and versions: read from the CSS headers of linux-firmware 20260309's
  i915/tgl_guc_70.1.1.bin (sw_version 70.1.1, uCode 277056 bytes, RSA 256) and
  i915/tgl_huc.bin; the same parser gives 70.49.4 / 334976 bytes for
  tgl_guc_70.bin, which matches the live record of the captured host.
- The live record of that host (captured 2026-10-16 as root with capture.sh in a
  `docker run --privileged --network none -v /:/host:ro` container) reads
  "GuC firmware: i915/tgl_guc_70.bin / status: RUNNING / version: found 70.49.4";
  the huc_info here is that record unchanged.

Not from hardware: the stale firmware state itself (by construction). allocatable
and env are raptorlake-nvidia's.
